                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><b>Message of the Chief Project Officer (CPO)</br>
Construction and Maintenance Division (CMD)</b>
</br>
</br>
<p>It gives me immense pleasure to present an overview of the activities and achievements of the Construction and Maintenance Division (CMD) at Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU).</br>

The University’s infrastructure is entrusted with the CMD for developing, maintaining, and upgrading the physical assets of IGNOU—both at the Headquarters in Maidan Garhi to AGVC, New Delhi, and at Regional Centres across the country. This division ensures that the academic, administrative, and residential building facilities are not only functional but also sustainable, energy-efficient, and conducive to a vibrant teaching-learning environment.</br>

Over the years, CMD has successfully executed numerous construction projects, including Regional Centre buildings across India, residential complexes, academic blocks, convention centres, and supporting infrastructure. We also provide uninterrupted essential services such as water supply, sewage treatment, electrical sub-stations, and centralized air-conditioning plants, while simultaneously focusing on renewable energy adoption, rainwater harvesting, and eco-friendly initiatives.</br>

In line with the University’s vision, CMD is committed to sustainable growth. With the integration of solar energy systems, LED lighting, water recycling, and green construction practices. Several upcoming projects—including new academic, residential, and student-centric facilities—are designed to further strengthen IGNOU’s infrastructure and enhance the learning experience of our students.</br>

I take this opportunity to appreciate the relentless efforts of my colleagues and staff in CMD, whose dedication ensures the smooth functioning of our campuses nationwide. Together, we reaffirm our commitment to creating a modern, sustainable, and learner-friendly campus that reflects IGNOU’s pioneering spirit in distance education.</br>

</br>

Er. Rattan Singh</br>
Chief Project Officer (CMD)</br>
Construction and Maintenance Division</br>
IGNOU, New Delhi</br></p>
