                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-5" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Campuses"  ><center><b><h4>Details of the Campus</h4></b></center>

<p><b>i) Landscape of IGNOU Campus</b></br>

The IGNOU campus at Maidan Garhi, New Delhi, is spread across 150 acres and has been developed as a self-contained institutional township. The campus landscape is designed to maintain an eco-friendly and green environment:</br><ul>

<li>Large open green areas and lawns maintained through treated water from STPs.</li>
<li>Rainwater harvesting pits located across the campus for groundwater recharge.</li>
<li>Dedicated horticulture section for plantation and maintenance of gardens.</li>
<li>Internal road network with avenues of trees for a pollution-free environment.</li>
<li>Walking tracks and open spaces for students, faculty, and staff.</li></ul></p>

<p><b>ii) Regional Centres Owning Permanent Campuses</b></br>

IGNOU has successfully constructed 21 Regional Centre buildings across India, with built-up areas ranging from 500 sqm to 4900 sqm, while a few more are in process for construction.</br>

Regional Centres with their own campuses (completed):</br><ul>

<li>Aizawl</li>
<li>Jodhpur</li>
<li>Rajkot</li>
<li>Trivandrum</li>
<li>Ahmedabad</li>
<li>Bhubaneswar</li>
<li>Bhopal</li>
<li>Cochin</li>
<li>Jaipur</li>
<li>Karnal</li>
<li>Lucknow</li>
<li>Madurai</li>
<li>Patna</li>
<li>Raipur</li>
<li>Shillong</li>
<li>Agartala</li>
<li>Bangalore</li>
<li>Jammu</li>
<li>Noida</li>
<li>Pune</li>
<li>Port Blair</li></ul></p>
</br>

<b>Regional Centres are in process for construction:</b><ul>

<li>Vijayawada (under construction)</li> 
<li>Imphal</li>
<li>Itanagar</li>
<li>Nagpur</li></ul>


<p><b>iii) Technical Infrastructure of the Campus</b></br>

The CMD maintains a robust technical infrastructure to ensure uninterrupted facilities for the university community:</br>

<b>Sewage Treatment Plants (STPs)</b><ul>
<li>Multiple STPs operational within the campus.</li>
<li>Capacity to treat over 1,00,000 litres per day.</li>
<li>Treated water is reused for horticulture and landscaping.</li></ul>
</br>
<b>Water Reservoirs & Supply</b></br><ul>

<li>10 Tube Wells connected to dedicated pump houses.</li>
<li>Supplementary water supply through Delhi Jal Board pipelines.</li>
<li>Underground water reservoirs for storage and campus-wide distribution.</li></ul>
</br>
<b>Solar Power System</b><ul>

<li>500 kWp rooftop solar panels installed on RESCO mode, grid-connected.</li>
<li>Further expansion planned through SECI empanelled agencies as per MNRE norms.</li>
<li>Contribution towards green energy and reduced carbon footprint.</li></ul>
</br>

<b>Electrical Sub-stations</b></br><ul>

<li>Multiple 11 KV substations operational in the campus.</li>
<li>Recent upgradation of Substation No. 4 & 5 through CPWD.</li>
<li>Ensures uninterrupted power supply to academic, residential, and service buildings.</li></ul>
</br>

<b>Air Conditioning Plants (AC Plants)</b></br><ul>

<li>Centralized AC plants are serving the Academic Blocks, Convention Centre, Vice-Chancellor Office, VIP Guest House, and EMPC.</li>
<li>Replacement of AC plants at Block–15 and Academic Complex, Convention Centre has been completed.</li>
<li>Regular operation and maintenance is being carried out for A.C Plants through CPWD.</li></ul>

<p><b>iv) Civil & Electrical Maintenance</b></br>

The Construction & Maintenance Division (CMD) ensures the civil and electrical upkeep of all major university facilities, including:</br><ul>

<il>Convention Centre – AC plants, electrical systems, and structural maintenance.</il>
<il>Staff Quarters at MGRC & AGVC – routine repair, renovation, and utility services.</il>
<il>Guest Houses – upkeep of civil structures, interiors, electrical systems, and essential services for visiting dignitaries and faculty.</il>
<il>Vice-Chancellor’s Building – complete maintenance of civil and electrical works including support utilities.</il>
<il>Temporary and Permanent Campus at Headquarters (Maidan Garhi, New Delhi) – structural and electrical upkeep of academic blocks, office complexes, and residential facilities.</il>
<il>Regional Centre Buildings across India – routine maintenance of civil structures, substations, water systems, and electrical installations.</il></ul></p>
 
